# Ordering does NOT matter here. vsce does not resolve these rules in order:
# a `!` line re-includes everything it matches no matter where it sits, and no
# exclusion anywhere in this file overrides it. Verified by widening
# `!client/out/extension.js` to `!client/out/**` — every `.map` under it was
# packaged, straight past the `**/*.map` rule at the bottom.
#
# So the "never ship" rules at the end are a reading aid, not a backstop, and
# the only real protection is keeping every negation as narrow as the one file
# it needs to re-admit. Widen one and it silently ships whatever it now covers.

# --- Development-only files -------------------------------------------------
.vscode/**
.github/**
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.editorconfig
eslint.config.mjs
scripts/**
docs/**
samples/**
samples-notebook/**
images/icon.svg
# The demo still, which the README shows by URL and not out of the package: the
# Marketplace resolves a README image over https, so shipping it would be weight
# nothing in here reads. The film itself is a release asset and was never in the
# tree. Named on its own — images/ also holds the icons, and those must ship.
images/regelspraak-demo.png

# --- Dependencies -----------------------------------------------------------
# Neither tree ships. Both halves are bundled with their dependencies inlined:
# the client by scripts/bundle-client.mjs, the language server before it is
# staged in. This replaces a hand-maintained allowlist of runtime packages,
# which would have broken silently the first time a dependency of
# vscode-languageclient changed.
node_modules/**
client/node_modules/**

# Development build output. `client/out/extension.js` is overwritten by the
# bundle at packaging time and is the only file from here that ships.
client/out/**
!client/out/extension.js

# The client's manifest only describes dependencies that are now inlined;
# `main` resolves to the file above directly, so nothing reads these.
client/package.json
client/package-lock.json

# `server/` is staged at release time and must ship: the extension is
# non-functional without it.

# --- Never ship (grouped last for readability; see the note at the top) -----
**/*.ts
**/*.map
**/tsconfig.json
**/tsconfig.base.json
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.bin/**
